@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07: the refusals the capstone itself owns.
--
-- Each one marks a place where the household needs something no composed row
-- encodes, or where the text does not decide (GAPS.md lists the provisions, in
-- the order the capstone needs them; NOTES.md the forks). A refusal a ROW owns
-- is never restated here: it reaches the caller from the row, through its
-- adapter, in the row's own words.
--
-- This module imports no row, so the adapters and the pipeline can all use it.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 — the capstone's own refusals`

§§ `The period`

-- 2026 is the one period all six rows answer (NOTES.md section 3): IL-02 answers
-- tax years from 2024; IL-03's s 121 tax years 2026-2027 and s 121B from 2026;
-- IL-04 and IL-05 contribution months from January 2026, and 2027 only on
-- figures the caller supplies; IL-06 days from 1 May 2015 to 31 December 2026;
-- IL-01 any year for which the credit-point value is supplied.
@ref NOTES.md section 3, "The period"; the rows' own year gates
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 answers months of 2026 only, the one period all six composed rows answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 answers months of 2026 only, the one period all six composed rows answer"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07: a month of the year is numbered from 1 to 12` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07: a month of the year is numbered from 1 to 12"

§§ `The household`

@ref NOTES.md fork K4; BRIEF.md, "The household"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 composes a household with one earner; a spouse with taxable income is outside it` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 composes a household with one earner; a spouse with taxable income is outside it"

@ref NII Schedule K "שכר מינימום" (source line 4772), as row IL-05 reads it (its fork F11)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 holds Schedule K's minimum only for an employee to whom the full monthly minimum wage of an adult applies` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 holds Schedule K's minimum only for an employee to whom the full monthly minimum wage of an adult applies"

@ref NII s 342(c)(2) (source line 3662); Schedule A1 Part D (source lines 4431-4453), not encoded by any row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the earner is a woman, and the age Part D of Schedule A1 fixes for her is not given` MEANS
    REFUSE "the earner is a woman, and the age Part D of Schedule A1 fixes for her is not given"

§§ `The Income Tax Ordinance: what no row encodes`

-- ITO s 65 (source line 2448): a couple's income is the registered spouse's,
-- assessed in that spouse's name. Row IL-02 names it as an outcome and does not
-- compute it (its NOTES.md section 1).
@ref ITO s 65 (source lines 2447-2448), not encoded; row IL-02 NOTES.md section 1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no separate calculation governs the earner's tax, so the couple is assessed under section 65 of the Income Tax Ordinance, which is not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "no separate calculation governs the earner's tax, so the couple is assessed under section 65 of the Income Tax Ordinance, which is not encoded"

-- ITO s 40(b) (source lines 1632-1647): the credit points for the children of
-- a single-parent family, and the extra point of (1B) and (2).
@ref ITO s 40(b) (source lines 1632-1647), not encoded (row IL-08)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the credit points for the children of a parent without a spouse are given by section 40(b) of the Income Tax Ordinance, which is not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "the credit points for the children of a parent without a spouse are given by section 40(b) of the Income Tax Ordinance, which is not encoded"

-- The credits and deductions no composed row encodes (GAPS.md, items 4-5).
@ref ITO ss 35, 39A-40D, 44-47 (source lines 1572-1805), not encoded
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the earner has a credit or deduction under a provision of the Income Tax Ordinance no composed row encodes, such as section 35, 45A or 47` MEANS
    REFUSE "the earner has a credit or deduction under a provision of the Income Tax Ordinance no composed row encodes, such as section 35, 45A or 47"

-- ITO s 164 (source lines 5322-5324) withholds tax from salary "in the manner and
-- at the rates prescribed"; the Income Tax (Deduction from Salary and Wages)
-- Regulations 5753-1993 (noted at source line 5338) are not in the source bundle.
@ref ITO s 164 (source line 5323); the 5753-1993 Regulations (source line 5338), not in the source bundle; NOTES.md fork K1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 apportions the tax for the year to a month only where the salary is the same in every month; withholding under section 164 of the Income Tax Ordinance is not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 apportions the tax for the year to a month only where the salary is the same in every month; withholding under section 164 of the Income Tax Ordinance is not encoded"

-- NOTES.md fork K3: neither s 33A nor s 121B says whether credit points are set
-- off against the additional tax. Reached only where the credits exceed the
-- s 121 tax and there is additional tax, which no household of the capstone's
-- shape reaches; declined there rather than guessed.
@ref ITO s 33A (source line 1563), s 121B (source lines 4455-4465); NOTES.md fork K3
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the credits exceed the tax under section 121 and there is additional tax under section 121B; the text does not say whether credit points are set off against the additional tax` MEANS
    REFUSE "the credits exceed the tax under section 121 and there is additional tax under section 121B; the text does not say whether credit points are set off against the additional tax"

§§ `The National Insurance Law: what no row encodes`

-- NII s 72 (source lines 853-856): the months for which the allowance is paid.
-- Row IL-06 answers a day; it leaves the mapping of days to paid months to s 72
-- (its NOTES.md section 2).
@ref NII s 72 (source lines 853-856), not encoded; row IL-06 NOTES.md section 2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a child of the household is born, or turns 18, during the month; section 72 of the National Insurance Law decides which months are paid, and is not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "a child of the household is born, or turns 18, during the month; section 72 of the National Insurance Law decides which months are paid, and is not encoded"

§§ `Answers a row returned as a problem with the facts`

-- Row IL-03 returns LEFT for an amount of income, an inflationary amount, a
-- betterment or a sale value that is negative; of these only a negative salary
-- can arise from a household record.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-03 reports that the facts cannot describe a case: an amount is negative` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-03 reports that the facts cannot describe a case: an amount is negative"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-06 reports that the household's facts cannot describe a family on the day` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-06 reports that the household's facts cannot describe a family on the day"
